## API

The heredoc runs with the names of the API module's `__all__` bound, plus `name`. Its delimiter is quoted, so
the shell expands nothing inside it. `--repo` names the project the document belongs to, and the API writes
under it.

```
harness-skill-api --repo "$${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}" --file "$${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/${snake}_api.py" <name> <<'PY'
if not document_path(name).is_file():
    create(name)
document = add_entry(name, new_entry(kind="first", text="<entry text>"))
print(f"{document_path(name).as_posix()}: {len(document.entries)} entries")
PY
```
